WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.292 --> 00:00:03.375
(indistinct chatter)

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:07.351
(dramatic music)

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.693
- I was born in Texas.

00:00:16.693 --> 00:00:20.210
My mom ventured out when she was 18

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:23.980
to go to someplace
other than our hometown,

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.623
she ended up in Texas
where she met my father.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:30.080
She ended up getting pregnant with me

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:31.640
a couple of years later.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:36.553
My dad actually left while
my mom was having me.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:40.310
My mom was forced to go back to Indiana

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:42.673
with her parents where I grew up.

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:47.620
She raised me alone.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.130
You know, she was a single parent.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:52.770
She did a really great job at raising me.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:54.600
You know, I had morals and ethics

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.800
and I learned how to treat people

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.600
the way that I wanted to be treated.

00:00:59.542 --> 00:01:02.390
I was a really bad kid,

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:03.960
I was always getting in trouble

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.970
because I didn't have a
male role model in my life

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:09.350
to give me any kinda discipline I think.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:12.630
And by the time I was 12,

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.420
I was getting kicked out of school,

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.330
and getting in trouble all the time,

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:17.840
and getting put on probation,

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.822
and different things like that.

00:01:19.822 --> 00:01:21.290
(clears throat)

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:24.160
When my father came back
when I was 12 years old,

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.080
and he came back for a
very short period of time

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:29.060
where he was trying to be,
trying to be back in my life,

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:33.100
but he ended up just passing away,

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.193
like from a heart failure.

00:01:35.193 --> 00:01:38.160
My mom was left to raise me by herself,

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.000
you know, and she did
the best that she could,

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.273
but I was a really bad kid.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:47.970
I was 16 when I started using drugs

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:52.120
because I was, I had a injury to my leg.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:57.700
I was in a pretty bad car accident.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:00.130
And I was also in a, ooh!

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:02.640
Was also in a, I had a football injury

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.980
where I blew my other knee out.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:09.610
So I got on to pain
medication at that time,

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:14.610
when I started using Vicodins,

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:16.070
and different things like that,

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:18.330
just to, you know, to ease the pain

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:19.430
I thought is was what I was doing,

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.470
but I didn't realize it was gonna cause

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:23.063
so many problems later on.

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:29.633
My mom was diagnosed with
cancer when I was 17,

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:33.670
she ended up beating that
first round of cancer,

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:38.527
but she also passed away a few years later

00:02:38.527 --> 00:02:41.433
from cancer as well
when I was incarcerated.

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:44.440
I was 18 years old

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:47.173
when I've caught my
first charge as an adult.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:51.743
I was just literally like one
week into my 18th birthday.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:55.380
I didn't wanna go to jail.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.510
I got caught with
Vicodin, ooh, not Vicodin,

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:02.510
I call it ecstasy, and
other pain pills as well.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:05.393
They sentenced me to do
two years on probation,

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:08.793
but I violated within a year,

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:14.050
and I took off and didn't really come back

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:16.853
until I was in my mid twenties.

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:23.047
My family exported drugs
from another country

00:03:23.047 --> 00:03:24.593
when I was in Portugal.

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:27.800
And I always wondered what
my dad's side of the family

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:28.820
did for a living.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:30.720
They drove very expensive cars,

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:32.840
and never went, never worked,

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:35.540
and never went to a nine to five job.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:37.860
And I always asked them
like, what they did,

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.680
you know, what, how do
they support themselves?

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.122
And I found out later on

00:03:42.122 --> 00:03:45.000
that my family was manufacturing

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.683
a drug called Methaqualone,
which is Quaaludes,

00:03:49.611 --> 00:03:53.430
for another name for those as Quaaludes.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:55.930
When I was on the run
from my first charge,

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:58.670
I was able to get out of the country

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:00.060
and moved to Portugal

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:04.083
where I learned how to
manufacture this drug.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:09.030
And I did that for, for
many years, for seven years,

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:12.420
until my uncle passed
away from cancer as well,

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:16.650
left me, you know, I planned
on making millions of dollars,

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:19.410
and being able to retire
at a very young age,

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:22.403
but it just didn't end
up working out that way.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:28.150
When he passed away, I was
kinda left with nothing.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:31.440
My, his wife took all the chemicals,

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.770
and all the glassware and
ended up selling it to somebody

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:36.900
that was outside of my family.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:41.240
And I was left to
basically my own devices,

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:45.700
no money, no way to make a dollar,

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:47.941
I didn't know what I was gonna do.

00:04:47.941 --> 00:04:49.563
So I went back home,

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:54.513
ended up catching another
charge for possession.

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:59.970
When I went into that last
time that I spent in jail,

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:03.560
I was doing a two year,
doing one sentence.

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:07.423
And I met a guy in there
who talks about heroin.

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:09.700
And I always thought that heroin

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:12.530
was like the biggest no-no,

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:14.752
the biggest thing that you shouldn't do.

00:05:14.752 --> 00:05:18.096
And anybody that did it, was just like,

00:05:18.096 --> 00:05:20.163
you know, not a good person.

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:25.460
But when I got out of jail,

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:29.195
I hit that person up and
he offered to take me

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:32.950
to another state to go
get some heroin one day,

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:36.650
which I thought about it for a while,

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:40.413
but I ended up going
and driving him to Ohio,

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:43.680
which is where we were gonna go

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:45.293
and get this heroin I guess.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:51.280
When, the first time I tried heroin,

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:54.350
like, it was like the greatest thing

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:57.760
that's ever been created by God.

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:02.760
You know, it was something that
it changed my life entirely.

00:06:05.755 --> 00:06:08.470
It was like a warm hug from my mom,

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:10.350
from my mother, you know,

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:11.700
it sort of reminded me of something

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:15.450
that just like kept me warm and fuzzy.

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:18.670
And it made me feel like there was like,

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:22.853
never gonna be anything else
that there was any better.

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:28.970
So at that time I was
living in a small town

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:32.122
where nobody really did heroin,

00:06:32.122 --> 00:06:35.700
they were smoking pot and eating pills,

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:36.660
and doing things like that.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:39.100
But when I discovered heroin,

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.920
I thought it was the
greatest thing in the world.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:43.120
And so I wanted all my friends to try it,

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:45.010
you know, and all my friends to experience

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:48.220
what I was experiencing as well.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:52.030
So I brought my first few bags of heroin

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:54.500
into this little small town,

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:57.010
where everybody knows who you are.

00:06:57.010 --> 00:07:02.010
And it's a pretty, pretty crazy to think

00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:05.330
that like, within like a year's time,

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:07.690
I was just like known
as like the heroin king,

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:09.243
of this little small town.

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:12.490
Like every, I had everybody coming to me

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:15.440
and getting bags and like I started

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:16.830
to getting watched by the police,

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:20.323
and things were going
downhill pretty quickly,

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:22.860
cause I was using all the time,

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:27.860
and constantly like trying
to figure out what's next

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:32.554
and living the lifestyle

00:07:32.554 --> 00:07:36.980
like a rockstar almost, in my opinion.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:41.980
Like I had a awesome car,
had a beautiful girlfriend,

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:44.080
tons of money.

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:46.540
And I was just living what I thought

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:48.190
was gonna be the rest of my life.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.870
But again, it just didn't turn out that,

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:54.483
it didn't turn out the
way that I expected it to.

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:03.180
I got arrested for something,
it's pretty petty, my opinion,

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:07.020
it was just a Vicodin.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:09.210
And when I got charges of Vicodin,

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:12.963
I got sentenced to do one sentence,

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:16.630
but it was a suspended due to probation,

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:19.370
and different things, that I
had to complete for classes,

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:20.803
and things like that.

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:26.113
I ended up meeting my
wife shortly after that.

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:29.500
She didn't want me to go to jail.

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:33.510
So I ended up moving into
her little small town.

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:36.410
We started selling
heroin to all the people

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:38.103
in that small town also.

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:44.573
The wife that I met was
something that was like,

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:50.460
she was 19, I was 25, something like that,

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:53.853
24 or 23, something in that area.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:57.183
And I just fell in love with her.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:02.170
And she was like my little
Bonnie and Clyde, I guess,

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:05.220
we were just going out and
doing destructive shit,

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:09.130
and buying heroin and
selling it to all her friends

00:09:09.130 --> 00:09:11.953
and, you know, making lots of money.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:15.833
But we both had a terrible habit.

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:20.530
Pretty shortly after that, the police came

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:23.910
to her little small town
where I was living in,

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:28.380
and ended up arresting me
for a violation of probation

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:30.533
that I had and just took me to jail.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:34.070
When I got incarcerated
for that last time,

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:37.000
it was a pretty hard because my mom,

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:39.210
who is the only parent that I've ever had,

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:41.373
was diagnosed with cancer again.

00:09:42.492 --> 00:09:44.573
She, they only gave her a year to live,

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:47.890
and I was gonna have to do a year in jail.

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:52.653
I did most of that time.

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:56.510
Like I was on a work release program.

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:59.210
So I was out in the world every day

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:02.070
and life wasn't so bad,

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:05.680
until I ended up catching
my wife cheating on me

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:07.263
with one of my closest friends.

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:13.690
She ended up actually trying to turn me in

00:10:13.690 --> 00:10:15.980
to get me to do more jail time.

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:18.200
She'd met me, she met me somewhere

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:20.300
when I was on work release
and dropped off some things

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:24.190
for me to bring back
into the work release.

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:26.590
And she called the police and told them

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:28.620
that I was bringing things in,

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:32.350
and I almost got sentenced
to another 10 years or so

00:10:32.350 --> 00:10:34.050
for bringing things into the jail.

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:39.400
Luckily I, smart enough
to kinda figure out

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:43.987
how to sit and wait for,
to get my opportunity

00:10:43.987 --> 00:10:46.130
to get rid of what I needed to get rid of,

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:48.793
so that I wouldn't end up
having to do that time.

00:10:50.686 --> 00:10:53.580
They, I sat in jail for
probably nine months

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:54.413
out of that year.

00:10:54.413 --> 00:10:56.814
And they sent me to go to a rehab.

00:10:56.814 --> 00:10:57.840
I went to my first rehab

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:00.563
which was at a mental hospital in Indiana.

00:11:03.157 --> 00:11:06.043
Was there for a month,

00:11:06.043 --> 00:11:08.380
at that time, that's when
I went to the hospital

00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:11.090
and my mom, and the doctor,

00:11:11.090 --> 00:11:13.570
and the families and everything was there.

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:17.630
And they told her that she
didn't have very long to live,

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:20.693
like weeks, two months,
something like that.

00:11:22.326 --> 00:11:27.326
I was very angry and didn't
really know what I was gonna do,

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:32.810
but the rehab was extremely
not receptive for me

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:35.980
to going and seeing her.

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:40.380
So they escorted me to
the hospital in handcuffs

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:42.500
and would not leave the room

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:46.293
for my last visit with my
mom, it was really hard.

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:49.410
They escorted me back to the rehab.

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:52.343
And at that time, my wife showed up,

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:56.920
and she was, told me that
it was my birthday actually.

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:59.410
And she told me that she showed up,

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:02.170
she was extremely late
three, four hours late.

00:12:02.170 --> 00:12:04.470
And when she showed up,
she was all fucked up.

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:08.110
I made her pull her arm, her sleeves up,

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:11.330
and that's when I found out
she was using heroin again.

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:13.740
And I ended up getting into a fight

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:15.950
with one of the people at the rehab

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:18.100
because I just found out my mom

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:20.700
was gonna have a few weeks left to live.

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:23.700
I just found out my wife
was using heroin again.

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:28.064
And that's when I kinda snapped, you know,

00:12:28.064 --> 00:12:30.760
and beat one of the guys
that was working there,

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:31.673
half to death.

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:35.030
They took me in a room

00:12:35.030 --> 00:12:36.320
that I didn't know what was gonna happen.

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:39.250
And then they sent me back
to jail the very next day.

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:42.123
No credited time of the
months that I've been there,

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:47.430
And when I went home or
when I went back to jail,

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:49.810
I had no idea when I
was gonna be released.

00:12:49.810 --> 00:12:52.743
No idea when my mom was gonna pass away.

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:55.890
And I actually got sentenced

00:12:55.890 --> 00:12:57.943
to do another nine months in jail.

00:12:59.089 --> 00:13:04.089
At that time, I had nobody
putting money on my books.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:06.230
I had nobody helping me.

00:13:06.230 --> 00:13:09.980
So I was angry, I was hungry,

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:14.430
and I was doing what
I had to do to get by.

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:19.430
I had some guy there, who was
a, I'll never forget this,

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:23.100
he ended up, there was a time

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:24.070
where we were switching out

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:26.160
this ice bucket in the jail,

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:27.680
cause we had like one ice bucket a day,

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.210
that we could use for the whole day.

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:31.760
When this guy came up to me

00:13:31.760 --> 00:13:33.932
and ask why I was
changing this ice bucket,

00:13:33.932 --> 00:13:37.780
and he spilled a whole
cup of water over my head.

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:41.290
And he was laughing and
thinking it was hilarious.

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:45.130
And I just turned red.

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:48.453
I couldn't see anything
besides blood, man.

00:13:49.604 --> 00:13:50.930
And I started fighting this guy

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:52.540
and I got him on the ground

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:56.140
and beat him until he
was flat black and blue.

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:58.740
And the police ran, you
know, police came in

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:01.470
and ended up putting me
in solitary confinement

00:14:01.470 --> 00:14:04.304
for six months.

00:14:04.304 --> 00:14:05.970
I did a cell by myself.

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:08.190
No idea of anything.

00:14:08.190 --> 00:14:10.380
Like I had no money to order if anything,

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:14.150
no commissary, no nothing, no phone calls.

00:14:14.150 --> 00:14:16.053
It was just me in a cell by myself,

00:14:17.038 --> 00:14:22.038
and around nine months or so later,

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:29.240
like I had a, they just
came into my cell one day

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:31.400
and told me to pack my stuff up.

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:33.610
And I had no idea why
or what was going on,

00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:35.583
but I was being released.

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:39.290
And when they released me and
my grandparents were there,

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:42.710
and they took me back to
their house where my mom was,

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:46.080
and I got to spend a few hours with her

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:47.730
before she ended up passing away.

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:52.110
When she passed away,
she left me some money

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:54.650
so that I could take care
of myself for, you know,

00:14:54.650 --> 00:14:57.180
it's supposed to be a
longer period than it was,

00:14:57.180 --> 00:15:02.180
but I ended up spending all
the money on drugs, on heroin.

00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:12.600
At that time, my wife got a job.

00:15:12.600 --> 00:15:16.010
We were working, both
working at a a gold place

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:18.823
where I was flying a sign
for like eight hours a day.

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:24.530
She ended up getting a job
inside with the gold place,

00:15:24.530 --> 00:15:28.910
and ended up, she ended up like,

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:30.480
ended up sleeping with the guy

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:32.980
that was running this gold shop.

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:35.683
So that's what kinda
split our relationship up.

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:40.670
I got back with her again, later on.

00:15:40.670 --> 00:15:45.180
And on Thanksgiving, I
was busy with my family

00:15:45.180 --> 00:15:48.580
because you know, my family
didn't accept my wife

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:50.540
and my, they didn't, her family

00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:52.060
didn't really like me either.

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:54.230
So we were doing separate Thanksgivings.

00:15:54.230 --> 00:15:59.030
And I got, I went and did my
family thing and came home.

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:02.040
And when I came home, I got a phone call

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:04.350
from our friend's girlfriend,
that was telling me

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:08.880
that my wife was sleeping
with her husband, right now.

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:11.660
And I, the whole time I thought
she was with her family,

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:16.520
but I ended up going to where they were

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:19.533
and beating this guy, half to death.

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:23.960
My wife got into a fight with a girlfriend

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:25.060
of this other gentleman.

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:28.153
And that was kinda the
end of our relationship.

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:34.020
After my wife, I caught her with my friend

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:38.320
and luckily he didn't call,
I mean, the police came,

00:16:38.320 --> 00:16:39.660
they were on the way as I was leaving.

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:41.630
I could hear them coming.

00:16:41.630 --> 00:16:44.720
And I luckily I got away
and went back to my house

00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:48.020
and I called my aunt who
lives here in Los Angeles

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:50.270
and I told her what was going on.

00:16:50.270 --> 00:16:52.593
And she flew me out here to LA.

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:57.460
Shortly after that my wife had called me

00:16:57.460 --> 00:17:02.460
and told me she was pregnant,
and that it was my kid.

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:06.170
So I told her that I
would be there for her

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:07.780
as much as I could.

00:17:07.780 --> 00:17:10.870
And if the kid was mine, that
I would go back to Indiana

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:12.070
and I would be with her.

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:14.330
Nine months passed,

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:19.162
and not only was the child,
not my friends or mine,

00:17:19.162 --> 00:17:21.580
The child came out black,

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:23.480
not that I'm racist or anything at all,

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:26.853
but it was definitely
not my child, you know.

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:32.303
So needless to say, that
was the end of my marriage.

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:38.490
I was broken, man, like lost my wife,

00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:42.430
lost my mother, all
within like a year span.

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:47.430
And I started using heroin really heavy.

00:17:49.279 --> 00:17:52.560
My aunt here is like a saint, man.

00:17:52.560 --> 00:17:54.510
Like she's done everything
that she's could

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:58.560
to like try to get me
out of the drug game,

00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:00.710
and trying to get me on a normal path.

00:18:00.710 --> 00:18:03.993
But it's just not just not happened.

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:07.690
She's had me in and out of
rehabs and different places

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:10.820
that she thought was gonna change me,

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:13.780
but I always ended up back on the streets,

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:15.860
back using drugs and selling drugs,

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:18.783
and in and out of jail.

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:26.883
Since then, I've moved on to fentanyl,

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:31.520
heroin just wasn't
doing it for me anymore.

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:34.380
You know, I was doing black
tar heroin at the time,

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:38.020
and it just wasn't, it wasn't
getting me to the point

00:18:38.020 --> 00:18:40.020
where it was when I first started using.

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:45.330
Fentanyl, took me right
back to that first time

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:46.233
that I did heroin.

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:50.993
You know, it gave me
everything I was looking for,

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:56.483
but it's also ruined my life, man.

00:18:57.690 --> 00:18:59.740
I've not been able to do anything

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:04.080
besides sell drugs and lie
to my family ever since.

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:14.333
I've been homeless for
the first time this year.

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:18.500
Six months ago I had $50,000 in the bank.

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:21.714
I was selling fentanyl to everybody

00:19:21.714 --> 00:19:25.140
that had ever heard of
it, you know, (laughs)

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:30.140
But pandemic hit, after the pandemic hit,

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:35.390
I was just unemployed.

00:19:35.390 --> 00:19:40.390
I started using drugs even
heavier than I ever had before.

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:46.174
Kinda left now trying to figure out

00:19:46.174 --> 00:19:47.653
what's next.

00:19:49.233 --> 00:19:54.070
You know, so I've been homeless
now for just a few months,

00:19:54.070 --> 00:19:55.340
staying with some friends,

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:58.780
but I still consider myself homeless.

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:01.033
I'm in a place that I
really don't wanna be,

00:20:02.743 --> 00:20:05.523
dealing with people that
I don't wanna deal with,

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:08.800
you know spending time on Skid Row

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:11.190
for the first time in my life,

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:14.513
where I would never have
thought that I would ever be.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:21.733
And I'm basically just waiting
to figure out what's next.

00:20:23.165 --> 00:20:26.610
And I hope that something
eventually changes

00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:31.600
so that I can stop using this
drug, man, cause I hate it.

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:35.960
I hate the way it's made me become.

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:38.900
I don't care about anything
besides staying well,

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:41.283
and trying to put a roof over my head.

00:20:44.563 --> 00:20:46.623
That's about where I'm at today.

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:51.960
- [Male] Arthur, thank you so
much for sharing your story.

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:53.200
- Yeah.

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:54.090
- [Male] Good luck with everything, man.

00:20:54.090 --> 00:20:56.390
- Thanks man, I appreciate it.
- You've been through a lot.

00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:57.840
- I'm sure there's more to come

00:20:57.840 --> 00:21:00.833
but I hope I can get through
all this bullshit, man.

00:21:03.703 --> 00:21:04.536
- [Male] I know.

00:21:04.536 --> 00:21:05.463
Thank you.
- All right, thanks.

